   "at": "Overview.bs:5018-5022 #comparing-color-values",
   "quote": "Note: Two colors that are expressed in different <<color-space>>s\nbut are colorimetrically identical—for example,\n''red'' and ''color(display-p3 0.91748756 0.20028681 0.13856059)''—are [=equivalent colors=]\nby step 4 of this algorithm,\nsince they convert to the same ''oklab'' value."
  },
  {
   "id": "css4-0127",
   "kind": "explicit-statement",
   "input": "color(display-p3 1 1 1)",
   "expected": "white",
   "precision": null,
   "src": "css4",
   "at": "Overview.bs:5155-5158 #comparing-color-values",
   "quote": "<div class=\"example\" id=\"ex-equivalent-oklab-epsilon\">\n<span class=\"swatch\" style=\"--color: rgb(100% 100% 100%)\"></span>&nbsp;''color(display-p3 1 1 1)''\nand <span class=\"swatch\" style=\"--color: rgb(100% 100% 100%)\"></span>&nbsp;''white''\nare [=equivalent colors=]."
  },
